(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#" :text "Build and validate the native stage-1 compiler cache. The cached compiler is keyed by the actual asl1 import closure, the host library, the clang version, and asl1 source. A warm build rehashes the closure recorded with the entry and never interprets asl1; only a missing, stale or corrupt entry asks the interpreter for the closure.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#baseHashes" :text "base names compiler and library digests; the closure alone may change beneath the same base")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#singleFlight!" :text "separate flock guard serializes stale-owner inspection/removal and creation.\nThe requested lock file is created with O_EXCL and stores its owner PID. A")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/asl1Cache.asl#warmBinary!" :text "warm path: the head names the last key for this base; rehashing its recorded closure proves the key without interpreting asl1")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/auditCmd.asl#" :text "Pure AgentScript CLI audit command handler and query engine under ADR D98")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/batch.asl#" :text "Pure AgentScript native batch evaluator engine and RPC wire contract implementation.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/build.asl#" :text "asl build FILE [-o OUT]: asl-host checks FILE, cached native asl1 lowers it to LLVM IR (the interpreter is an explicit fallback), and clang links it with libaslrt.a into OUT, then libaslhost.a beside it when the program calls an unrouted sys, socket, parMap or parFold builtin; the temporary directory never outlives the command")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/build.asl#hostArchive?" :text "The IR text calls a C table only the host archive links: asl_rt_builtin_sys or asl_rt_builtin_sysNet (sys.c and sysNet.c, which left libaslrt.a in SYSLOWER-b) or asl_rt_builtin_parallel (parallel.c, which left it in PARASL). asl1 routes those sys, socket, parMap and parFold calls to ASL functions on a host libc.asl verifies, so such a build calls none; on any other host they stay C table calls.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/build.asl#linkLibs!" :text "The archives after the IR: libaslrt.a, whose member gcAsl.o is the program's collector (asl-target-llvm/gcRoute's module, GCASL-2), then the host archive when hostArchive? finds a call of a C table only it links; a missing host archive is ERR_BUILD.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/build.asl#findClang!" :text "command -v: a path with a slash names itself")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/build.asl#parseArgs!" :text "err carries the exit code after its message")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/build.asl#drop!" :text "rm -rf, but a failed removal is reported")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/build.asl#compileLl!" :text "no compiler source: the interpreter reports it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-cli/src/build.asl#hostLibOf" :text "libaslrt.a to libaslhost.a, libaslrt-asan.a to libaslhost-asan.a")
